\@writefile{loc}{\contentsline {added}{Added: \truncate {\Changestruncatewidth }{For the linear elastic case, Ambrosio--Tortorelli-type regularizations approximate the sharp-crack variational formulation in the sense of $\Gamma $-convergence as $\epsilon \to 0$. In this sense, the regularized fields $(\boldsymbol  {u},s)$ approximate the displacement field and crack set of the corresponding sharp-crack formulation, while the diffuse crack region represented by low values of $s$ approaches the crack set; no pointwise convergence statement for $s$ is intended here.}}{17}{section*.135}\protected@file@percent }
